@startuml
!theme materia

<style>
document {
  BackgroundColor transparent
  `materia wants Verdana, which isn't installed
  FontName sans-serif
}
</style>

title
  =Edge proxy as the Relying Party
  ==An AWS Application Load Balancer is shown
end title

actor "User\n(browser)" as browser
participant "Edge proxy\n(ALB)" as proxy
participant "Identity provider" as idp
participant "Stroom" as stroom

== The proxy runs the flow, once ==

browser -> proxy: GET /
proxy -> proxy: No session cookie
proxy --> browser: 302 to the //authorization endpoint//
browser -> idp: Sign in
idp --> browser: 302 to /oauth2/idpresponse\nwith an authorization code
browser -> proxy: GET /oauth2/idpresponse\ncode
proxy -> idp: POST //token endpoint//\nclient_id, client secret, code
idp --> proxy: ID token and access token
proxy -> idp: GET //userinfo endpoint//\naccess token
idp --> proxy: User claims
note right of proxy
  The ALB signs these claims,
  and discards the ID token.
  Only claims the userinfo
  endpoint returns reach Stroom
end note
proxy --> browser: Sets AWSELBAuthSessionCookie-*,\n302 to the original page

== Stroom verifies, on every request ==

browser -> proxy: GET / (session cookie)
proxy -> stroom: GET /\nx-amzn-oidc-data: signed claims JWT
stroom -> stroom: Verify the signature against the\nregional AWS key (cached),\ncheck signer and issuer,\nmap uniqueIdentityClaim to a Stroom user
note right of stroom
  The identity is never held in a
  Stroom session. It is re-derived
  from the header on every request,
  which is how the proxy's own
  token refresh reaches Stroom
end note
stroom --> proxy: Response
proxy --> browser: Response

@enduml
